From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mirko Vogt <foss@mirko.in>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: enable MFP for QCA99X0 firmware 10.4.1.00030-1

Set ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT despite no mfp support being
advertised by the firmware, based on exact firmware version and chip
type.

The QCA99X0 firmware in linux-firmware (10.4.1.00030-1, from around
2015), does not - unlike firmwares for similar chips - advertise the
"mfp" feature. As a result of missing mfp advertisement from firmware
side, ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT is not set and ath10k never sets the
PMF peer flag in WMI peer assoc for 802.11w peers.

Effect is heavily degraded throughput on the TX path (QCA99X0 as
AP -> STA, capped at a fraction of the RX path), when using 802.11w,
which e.g. is a requirement for wpa3.

However, the hardware itself appears to support mfp, as indicated by
alternative firmware projects, such as ath10k-ct, which advertises mfp
for QCA99X0.

Also the original firmware appears to actually support mfp, despite not
advertising it. Just assuming mfp support from the linux side and not
relying on advertised features, results in the TX path being on par with
the RX path.

Experienced and tested on an Aruba AP-325 running OpenWrt.

Tested-on: QCA99X0 hw2.0 PCI 10.4.1.00030-1 (Aruba AP-325)
Signed-off-by: Mirko Vogt <foss@mirko.in>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -2234,6 +2234,18 @@ static int ath10k_core_fetch_firmware_fi
 success:
 	ath10k_dbg(ar, ATH10K_DBG_BOOT, "using fw api %d\n", ar->fw_api);
 
+	/* QCA99X0 firmware 10.4.1.00030-1 does not advertise MFP support in
+	 * its firmware feature IE. Without the feature bit the PMF peer flag
+	 * is never passed to firmware for 802.11w peers.
+	 */
+	if (QCA_REV_99X0(ar) &&
+	    !strcmp(ar->normal_mode_fw.fw_file.fw_version, "10.4.1.00030-1")) {
+		ath10k_info(ar, "firmware %s does not advertise MFP support, enabling it\n",
+			    ar->normal_mode_fw.fw_file.fw_version);
+		__set_bit(ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT,
+			  ar->normal_mode_fw.fw_file.fw_features);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
